  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-240055</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uni.e.s pour l&apos;&#xe9;ducation et l&apos;emploi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Heavy-Duty Industrial Equipment and Commercial Vehicles (HDIECV) industry is key for the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)#s strategic productive sectors, including transport and logistics, mining, agriculture, forestry and construction; it is also one of the only industries where skilled labour needs are poised to increase in the medium-term.  The intervention aims to improve skills development and enhance youth employability in the HDIECV labour market in the Lualaba province. An increased supply of locally sourced skilled labour in the HDIECV industry will enhance productivity in the mining sector.  The project will contribute to establishing sustainable and scalable training programs in the transport and logistics sector.  Activities include skills needs assessment, developing educational materials, training trainers, transferring equipment, strengthening the training capacity of a selected training centre, creating a qualification framework, training young men and women (including existing professionals), piloting an AI solution for skills certification and improving coordination and cooperation between the private and the public sector in skills development (e.g. apprenticeships).  The project will be implemented in cooperation with Enabel.  It also seeks to create synergies and complement the PA</narrative>
  </description>
